# Side boxes (reference/components/block.md). Pages of 300 × 200 with margins of 20: page area of 260 × 160 from
# (20, 20), which ends at y = 180. Lines of 12 (Size 10) and 5 pt per character: a word of four letters and its
# space take 25, so a line of 260 holds 10 words, one of 190 (beside a box of 60 with a margin of 10), 7, one of
# 210 (beside a box of 40 with a margin of 10), 8, and one of 140 (between the two), 5.
#
# Section 1: img1 (60 × 60, right margin 10) at the left; p1 (14 words) and p2 (14 words) run beside it with 7
#   words per line (lines of 12 from 20 to 68), and p3 (20 words) starts at 68: its first line still overlaps the
#   box (which ends at 80) and has 7 words, the next two have the whole width, 10 and 3 words: 3 lines, 36.
# Section 2: in wrap, img2 (60 × 60, left margin 10) at the right and p4, 7 words, one line beside it; wrap
#   measures 60, the bottom of its side box, and below, a Block with a background, comes after it at 80.
# Section 3: l3 (60 × 60, right margin 10) at the left and r3 (40 × 100, left margin 10) at the right, both at the
#   top; p5 (45 words): 5 lines of 5 words between the two (up to 80), 2 of 8 beside r3 and the last one with 4.
# Section 4: sp (120) leaves 40 and img6 (60) does not fit: the break goes before it and page 5 starts with it and
#   p6 (14 words, 2 lines of 7). sp2 (90), which does not run beside it, goes below it, at 80, up to 170. img7
#   (60 × 8) fits in the 10 left, but the first line of p7 (7 words) does not: the break goes before the side box,
#   which goes with the line, and page 6 starts with both.
# Section 5: sp3 (100) and img8 (60 × 60) at 120, which fits exactly. p8 (60 words) has room for 5 lines, of 7
#   words beside the box; the rest, 25 words, is broken again on page 8 at the whole width: 10, 10 and 5.
